{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1075268-changing-the-dhampir","id":1075268,"title":"Changing the Dhampir","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-08T15:17:03-07:00","id":1075268,"title":"Changing the Dhampir","content":"One of the oddities of cWoD is the idea that Dhampir are a new thing when they have existed in Balkan folklore for centuries. I think that it would be interesting to have any sufficiently human female Kindred (Humanity 8+) to be able to bear Dhampir children without being 15th generation (exposure to Vitae, not genetics, should matter, so the father would be inconsequential). I think that it would give the Kindred of the Camarilla a reason to maintain their Humanity and be the reason why the Sabbat created the Revenants.<br /> <br /> The generation of the mother should be important to the Dhampir because they are constantly exposed to her blood for nine months. When they are killed by lethal damage, Dhampir would get a Stamina roll (difficulty mother's generation minus 10) to effectively be Embraced by their mother's blood. Other than that, they would gain other benefits from a low generation mother. Would you want to see a change in the Dhampir?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T15:54:05-07:00","id":1075284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1075268-changing-the-dhampir#post1075268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the oddities of cWoD is the idea that Dhampir are a new thing when they have existed in Balkan folklore for centuries.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;X existed in folklore&quot; is not a proof of existed. Jesus has existed in folklore for 2017 years now, but he's most likely a myth. Dragons have existed in folklore for much longer than that, but they are very definitely a myth. Even in WoD the myths are inaccurate and largely made up. Or there wouldn't be a masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T19:55:22-07:00","id":1075335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1075268-changing-the-dhampir#post1075268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the oddities of cWoD is the idea that Dhampir are a new thing when they have existed in Balkan folklore for centuries. I think that it would be interesting to have any sufficiently human female Kindred (Humanity 8+) to be able to bear Dhampir children without being 15th generation (exposure to Vitae, not genetics, should matter, so the father would be inconsequential). I think that it would give the Kindred of the Camarilla a reason to maintain their Humanity and be the reason why the Sabbat created the Revenants.<br /> <br /> The generation of the mother should be important to the Dhampir because they are constantly exposed to her blood for nine months. When they are killed by lethal damage, Dhampir would get a Stamina roll (difficulty mother's generation minus 10) to effectively be Embraced by their mother's blood. Other than that, they would gain other benefits from a low generation mother. Would you want to see a change in the Dhampir?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My familiarity with the Folklore is that its generally the male parent that is the Vampire not the female. That being said I go with the blood thickening/cylical Gehenna thing. There have been various points in history where &quot;this is the last generation of vampire&quot; was different than in the modern nights. SO during the Long Night and War of Princes 13th gens could make Dhampir. When Rome Fell perhaps 11th gens?<br /> <br /> Thus Dhampir are a sign of the time of thin blood and that a Gehenna is underway..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T20:35:33-07:00","id":1075342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1075268-changing-the-dhampir?p=1075284#post1075284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;X existed in folklore&amp;quot; is not a proof of existed. Jesus has existed in folklore for 2017 years now, but he's most likely a myth. Dragons have existed in folklore for much longer than that, but they are very definitely a myth. Even in WoD the myths are inaccurate and largely made up. Or there wouldn't be a masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragons exist six ways to Sunday in cWoD. They exist as Chimera in the Dreaming, Bygones and Spirits in the Middle and High Umbra, Plasmids in the Low Umbra, Zmei on the Earth, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T23:24:19-07:00","id":1075745,"title":"","content":"I would have the vampiric parent have to be male. I don't think that a living child could grow inside of an animated corpse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1129,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","user":"Sergeant Brother","date":". 04-04-2024, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T00:30:07-07:00","id":1075763,"title":"","content":"I was thinking back to this what about a third Option? Dhampir as &quot;Kinfolk&quot; to a third vampire type that come from particular biological lineages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T08:39:16-07:00","id":1075910,"title":"","content":"I'd maybe look at the Caitiffs as a means to have more historical dhampirs. As mentioned, &quot;Thin-Blood&quot; had a very different definition over the years, but Caitiffs seem to have happened throughout history. Every once in a while a Cainite just doesn't end up inheriting the clan affinities and weaknesses. I'd probably use that, with the logic that whatever mystical principle allows a Thin Blood to sire offspring works for a Caitiff too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T08:51:23-07:00","id":1075915,"title":"","content":"It would be easy enough to explain it as historically, tales of dhampyr come from misunderstandings about revenants. They're functionally the same thing, so in more modern times when individuals came about who actually <i>were</i> the half-mortal offspring of vampires they simply adopted the pre-existing name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T15:17:01-07:00","id":1076142,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that dhampyrs existed among the Kuei-jin centuries before the Time of Thin Blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Our society is held together by the thinnest of threads: that exquisitely refined sense of tribal order.<br /> Edith Wharton, The Age of Innocence<br /> <br /> I am a huge fan of both the Trinity Universe and the classic World of Darkness.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12799-spellfire22","name":"Spellfire22","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T04:56:12-07:00","id":1076907,"title":"","content":"well, we know that in the Dark Age, all the Clan embraced crazily for the intra and inter-clan wars (even before the Sabbat), so what about being a 15th Generation somehow survived and going around for centuries spawning damphir here and there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T07:38:46-07:00","id":1076961,"title":"","content":"Not to spoil or get ahead of myself.... isn't there something in BJD about Dhampires just kind of happening in the past, not being tied to gen 15, so you could have a dhampire born in the 1800's for example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4034-the_livewire","name":"The_Livewire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4034_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T08:06:30-07:00","id":1076976,"title":"","content":"Well, that is what I was thinking. While every 15th generation Kindred can make Dhampir, regardless of Humanity/Path, I was thinking that lower generation Kindred could only make Dhampir if they maintain sufficiently high Humanity (8+), were female, and spent an extra blood pool every dusk while pregnant to support the nascent Dhampir within them. It would make Dhampir very rare (the number of Kindred who are Humanity 8+, female, and are capable of spending two blood pool per evening while keeping Humanity 8+ probably number only a few hundred in the modern nights).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T12:28:48-07:00","id":1077129,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I did a write up on this a loooooong time ago (it's pretty clear from the tone of the writing that I was like 19) - it's still up on the salvaged <a href=\"http://bjz-backup.droppages.com/\" target=\"_blank\">BJ Zanzibar's WOD mirror site</a> (it's there on the front page). I believe 9 Humanity was required to father/mother a dhampir in that treatment, but I've long since decided (like you) that 8 Humanity is a better threshold.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The key notes:</span></span><ul><li>It's easier for male vampires to sire offspring. They only had to spend blood to mimic life functions for one scene to make their contribution.</li> <li>Female vampires COULD have children if their humanity was high enough, but it was a difficult process. They had to maintain their high humanity for the duration of the pregnancy and also expend one more blood each night to awaken (failing to do so, or running out of blood resulted in the vampire's body rejecting the fetus).</li> <li>It was therefore far more likely that a dhampir would be born from a human mother. The birth was likely to be incredibly taxing and difficult, so before the advent of modern medicine, mortality rates for a mortal mother during chidlbirth were very high.</li> <li>Because I allowed dhampir to be born from lower generation vampires, they each had an &quot;effective generation&quot; - the same as if they had been aired by their vampiric parent. So a 9th Generation vampire would produce a dhampir child with ab effective generation of 10th. This increased the dhampir's blood pool and allowed them to learn higher level disciplines than ghouls (possibly). It also made them immune to dominate from vampires of a higher generation than their effective gen.</li> <li>Dhampirs also had a &quot;Bloodright&quot; discipline that tried to mimic folkloric abilities like seeing invisible vampires or killing vampires with conventional weapons.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I'm currently working on an updated, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hXfco_lOvWmjOVY9yVXChT3WqALtnoVYcrWnOFJ-2Ig/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">unofficial supplement for Dhampirs</a> that updates some of these ideas but in a more &quot;V20&quot; and less &quot;amateur hour&quot; way. The rules aim to:</span></span><ul><li>Use the existing Dhampir mechanics as a jumping off point, but I expand on them using re-purposed &quot;Special Advantages&quot; rules from Ascension's right hand / bygone bestiary to give them the potential to &quot;unlock&quot; more vampiric traits. These traits are like special merits to help differentiate Dhampirs from Revenants or Ghouls.</li> <li>Detail the different ways Dhampirs might interact with Kindred society (so far only the Camarilla but I plan to talk about the Anarchs and Independents more, the Sabbat view Dhampirs as sacrilege - a debasement of Caine's blood) - these are similar to the Ghoul splats like Independant, Vassal and Revenant, but instead detail dhampirs who try (or have succeeded at) acclimating to Camarilla society, those who hunt vampires like the Dhampir of legend, and even those who try to pass themselves off as vampires. So far 3 of the 5 basic &quot;splats&quot; have write-ups.</li> <li>Discuss the Dhampirs of different clans (still in the early stages)</li> <li>Offer options for running everything from Time of Thin Blood-style &quot;Dhampirs are a modern phenomenon&quot; to a &quot;what if&quot; scenario where dhampir have been a part of vampiric society for a very long time (presenting them as the Camarilla's answer to Revenant families). The section for this isn't written yet, but the goal is to take the Gehenna-style &quot;sliding scale&quot; approach, while the default assumption is &quot;Dhampir *appear* to be a modern phenomenon but they may have existed in other times (a la V20 Dark Ages).</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Still a lot of work needed on this. The next section I plan on working on is re-purposing my old write-up to detail how lower generation vampires can produce Dhampir children - I definitely think I'll lower the Humanity threshold to 8, and specify that only those on Humanity can sire children in the mortal way. </span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5525-rebelwithoutaclan","name":"RebelWithoutAClan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5525_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T14:33:19-07:00","id":1077231,"title":"","content":"Vampire: The Requiem has a pretty compelling take on dhampirs (dampyrs) in Night Horrors: The Wicked Dead that isn't tied to thin-bloods. It's portable over to Masquerade without too much fuss.<br /> <br /> I particularly liked the part on male pregnancies:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Several mystical techniques permit vampires to breed<br /> with mortals. Some assist the user, and some allow the<br /> user to curse another so he\u2019ll unknowingly impregnate<br /> the next mortal with whom he has congress. Wait, you<br /> say, surely you mean that he\u2019ll impregnate the next<br /> mortal woman with whom he has congress, yes? Ha ha.<br /> No. Occult pregnancy is by its very nature a perversion<br /> of the essential human procreation\u2014a piratical invasion<br /> of something sacred and primal. Distinctions in what is<br /> and is not possible have already left the building, and<br /> that leaves us with female vampires impregnating women<br /> and male vampires impregnating men (with variations on<br /> these themes). While the woman carrying the child of<br /> her lesbian vampire lover would certainly be surprised at<br /> the development, she at least is biologically (and socially)<br /> equipped to contend with the life growing within her, the<br /> swell of belly and breast, the hormonal swings. She has<br /> the physical means for the baby to be born, as well.<br /> <br /> Pity her poor clueless male counterpart.<br /> <br /> Carrying pregnancy and giving birth is not something<br /> human males are biologically prepared for, nor socially con-<br /> ditioned to deal with. The parasitic Dampyr fetus that finds<br /> its own niche in a male abdominal cavity is protected by an<br /> occult placenta and cowl of tissue, but the male body it feeds<br /> upon is unprepared to handle the hormone flux, the swelling,<br /> the discomfort. It\u2019s a disconcerting experience, but compared<br /> to the (possibly fatal) agonies of delivery, the months of<br /> pregnancy seem like a fading nightmare. Surgery can save the<br /> father\u2019s life, but his sanity will be another matter. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:48:16-07:00","id":1077295,"title":"","content":"I actually had the opposite reaction to Requiem's dampyrs. I found the mechanics clunky, the treatment thematically stilted (the focus was so heavily weighed on &quot;we are the anti-vampires&quot; that the stories you can tell with the character type are severely limited), and dramatically... Well... Uninteresting. They seem more like sentient plot devices than characters inhabiting a story, at least based on the fiction and rules.<br /> <br /> That was my take on it anyway. I was really excited to read about them because I love dhampirs and wanted to see of there was anything I could crib for my house rules - sadly there wasn't anything evocative enough for me to port over to V:tM, but mileage may vary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5525,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5525-rebelwithoutaclan","user":"RebelWithoutAClan","date":".  Because mobile. 04-12-2017, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5525-rebelwithoutaclan","name":"RebelWithoutAClan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5525_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T01:09:00-07:00","id":1077567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryoga84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1075268-changing-the-dhampir?p=1076907#post1076907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, we know that in the Dark Age, all the Clan embraced crazily for the intra and inter-clan wars (even before the Sabbat), so what about being a 15th Generation somehow survived and going around for centuries spawning damphir here and there?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Because it was impossible to embrace 14th gen vampires then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T05:27:27-07:00","id":1077645,"title":"","content":"Could a 13th Generation vampire in the Dark Ages (who's blood was too thin to sire) produce a dhampir? Or had the blood not sufficiently thinned? (I suspect the latter but its interesting to think about)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5525-rebelwithoutaclan","name":"RebelWithoutAClan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5525_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T16:23:22-07:00","id":1078013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1075268-changing-the-dhampir?p=1077567#post1077567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Because it was impossible to embrace 14th gen vampires then.</div> </div> </div> </div>is this a written rule or some IC text?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T04:11:47-07:00","id":1078267,"title":"","content":"It's wasn't so much &quot;impossible&quot; as &quot;really, <i>really</i> rare&quot;. In Dark Ages, 13th gens are considered near-mythical and the flaw that makes you 13th generation strongly suggests also taking another flaw that means you can't embrace. So the bottom line is that it was nigh-unheard of for a 14th gen to even exist. <br /> <br /> That said, if the stars aligned...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T05:21:25-07:00","id":1078279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1075268-changing-the-dhampir?p=1078267#post1078267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's wasn't so much &quot;impossible&quot; as &quot;really, <i>really</i> rare&quot;. In Dark Ages, 13th gens are considered near-mythical and the flaw that makes you 13th generation strongly suggests also taking another flaw that means you can't embrace. So the bottom line is that it was nigh-unheard of for a 14th gen to even exist.<br /> <br /> That said, if the stars aligned...</div> </div> </div> </div>ok, that's the point. Because if was &quot;really&quot; impossible, would meant that &quot;rules&quot; (the rules of Embrace) change with time, and while 1000 years ago wasn't impossible to Embrace a 14th Generation, now we have 15th Generations... following this train of thoughts, in 500 years we could see 16th Generations and so on...<br /> <br /> anyway, my suggestion was actually that of a single 13th gen, almost randomly Embraced in that caothical time and unaware of her own generation (we see those a lot -mostly Caitiff- at that time were more rare, but not unheard) Embraced a child (so a 14th) or more than one. This &quot;waterblood&quot; Kindred could then generate Damphirs at will in the centuries between Dark Age and Masquerade. And go largely ignored because for him could be more simple to fake being human.<br /> In those centuries, wandering in the Balkans, his offsprings somehow originated the Dhampir myth (that many Tzimisce and Kindred-that-knows-Tzimisce disregarded as some Revenant thing).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T07:13:00-07:00","id":1078327,"title":"","content":"Why would any Lord allow Kindred of the 13th or higher generations to survive in their Domain. I do not think that it was mechanically impossible for a 14th or 15th generation to exist in the Dark Ages, I think that most Lords just killed off 13th generation Kindred (and their sires) when they were discovered because of the potential of 14th and 15th generation Kindred. Since most Kindred would not have met 13th generation Kindred, they would think that 14th and 15th generation Kindred were impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T07:37:26-07:00","id":1078344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryoga84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1075268-changing-the-dhampir?p=1078279#post1078279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> if was &quot;really&quot; impossible, would meant that &quot;rules&quot; (the rules of Embrace) change with time, and while 1000 years ago wasn't impossible to Embrace a 14th Generation, now we have 15th Generations... following this train of thoughts, in 500 years we could see 16th Generations and so on...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually something that is going to be discussed in Beckett's Jyhad Diary. There's a section that implies that 15th generation vampires have been able to sire for the first time, leading to a 16th generation (which has never existed before). Previously, in Time of Thin Blood, it was impossible (as stated in the rules) for 15th Generation vampires to sire childer (attempts failed and the subject died, invariably). I believe this was the case with 13th generation vampires in the original Vampire: The Dark Ages rulebook, but I don't have the books with me currently to verify that.<br /> <br /> In any case, the &quot;opening up&quot; of new generations as time marches on is a concept that exists in past rulebooks, and BJD is running with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5525-rebelwithoutaclan","name":"RebelWithoutAClan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5525_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T08:00:53-07:00","id":1078355,"title":"","content":"It's a progressive thing. A century or two before, 13th gen would probably have been &quot;absolutely no embrace ever&quot; and 12th gens would be the ones that were commonly thin blooded and all that. At the point Dark Ages is set, the 14 generation is just on the verge of becoming a thing, and probably can't embrace themselves. There's no flaw in the 20th Anniversary edition for playing one at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T14:45:09-07:00","id":1078543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1075268-changing-the-dhampir?p=1078327#post1078327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would any Lord allow Kindred of the 13th or higher generations to survive in their Domain. I do not think that it was mechanically impossible for a 14th or 15th generation to exist in the Dark Ages, I think that most Lords just killed off 13th generation Kindred (and their sires) when they were discovered because of the potential of 14th and 15th generation Kindred. Since most Kindred would not have met 13th generation Kindred, they would think that 14th and 15th generation Kindred were impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not exactly sayind a Kindred Lord would allow a 13th gen in his Domain, much more as having a 13th gen unaware of her Generation and actually skulking around trying to stay steer of every kindred more powerful than her (all in all, probably only the members of the High Clan proclaimed their Generation, most vampires would rather not tell if not pressed, and unless unsing Domination or blood ritual is difficult to tell exactly the Generation of some leech). Of course that will probably make her a Caitiff, but that's the (un)life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RebelWithoutAClan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1075268-changing-the-dhampir?p=1078344#post1078344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is actually something that is going to be discussed in Beckett's Jyhad Diary. There's a section that implies that 15th generation vampires have been able to sire for the first time, leading to a 16th generation (which has never existed before). Previously, in Time of Thin Blood, it was impossible (as stated in the rules) for 15th Generation vampires to sire childer (attempts failed and the subject died, invariably). I believe this was the case with 13th generation vampires in the original Vampire: The Dark Ages rulebook, but I don't have the books with me currently to verify that.<br /> <br /> In any case, the &quot;opening up&quot; of new generations as time marches on is a concept that exists in past rulebooks, and BJD is running with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, THIS is an interesting concept.<br /> And, staying in topic, would probably make it easier my theory.<br /> If, for example, in the Dark Age the &quot;limit&quot; is 12th Generation, then a 12th Generation &quot;could&quot; make Dhapirs, and there were surely a lot of 12th gen going around at that time.<br /> <br /> <br /> note to me: I should actually read what I buy<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1075268-changing-the-dhampir?p=1078355#post1078355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a progressive thing. A century or two before, 13th gen would probably have been &quot;absolutely no embrace ever&quot; and 12th gens would be the ones that were commonly thin blooded and all that. At the point Dark Ages is set, the 14 generation is just on the verge of becoming a thing, and probably can't embrace themselves. There's no flaw in the 20th Anniversary edition for playing one at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>all this reasonment probably deserve its own topic, it's an interesting concept<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-04T15:44:00-07:00","id":1533577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The_Livewire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1075268-changing-the-dhampir?p=1076961#post1076961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to spoil or get ahead of myself.... isn't there something in BJD about Dhampires just kind of happening in the past, not being tied to gen 15, so you could have a dhampire born in the 1800's for example?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually there is but it is extremly easy to be overread because it is a kind of Retcon/Rule update to a V20 Bane while another V20 Bane explicity states about this possibility.<br /> The first sentence about Dhampires rule wise is, that it may be extrem rarely but <b>Thinbloods</b> may get pregnant with mortal children. Later on it even states that Dhampires are those mortal children and yes even the vampire may get pregnant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T02:16:46-07:00","id":1536960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1075268-changing-the-dhampir#post1075268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the oddities of cWoD is the idea that Dhampir are a new thing when they have existed in Balkan folklore for centuries. I think that it would be interesting to have any sufficiently human female Kindred (Humanity 8+) to be able to bear Dhampir children without being 15th generation (exposure to Vitae, not genetics, should matter, so the father would be inconsequential). I think that it would give the Kindred of the Camarilla a reason to maintain their Humanity and be the reason why the Sabbat created the Revenants.<br /> <br /> The generation of the mother should be important to the Dhampir because they are constantly exposed to her blood for nine months. When they are killed by lethal damage, Dhampir would get a Stamina roll (difficulty mother's generation minus 10) to effectively be Embraced by their mother's blood. Other than that, they would gain other benefits from a low generation mother. Would you want to see a change in the Dhampir?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's your game, do what you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}